<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: logical, min,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function will determine if the user&#x27;s guess is a valid guess. That is, it an actual word in the dictionary.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>current_guess</pf> (string) number — is a five-letter string</p>
			<p><pf>dictionary_words</pf> (14854 5) number — is an array of strings, where each element in the array is a valid 5-letter word. In other words, this will serve as the "dictionary" of all 5-letter words.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>is_a_word</pf> (boolean) number — returns true (or 1) if the current guess matches with one of the dictionary words, and returns false (or 0) if the current guess if not among any of the words in the dictionary</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		INPUTS
		'LAMPS'
		dictionary_words
		OUTPUT
		1 (logical)
		INPUTS
		'ZZSUF'
		dictionary_words
		OUTPUT
		0 (logical)
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
